schema: "0.3"
id: char-005-mercurial-ash
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a concept artist for a hand-painted 2D isometric game inspired by
    Studio Ghibli and Stardew Valley. The visual style is painterly with visible
    brushstrokes, warm color temperatures, soft edges, and no pure black outlines.
    This character is deliberately species-ambiguous -- could be human, synthetic,
    or something else entirely. The mystery is the point.
  text: |
    Character portrait of Mercurial Ash, a traveling merchant of unknown species
    who appears in different settlements across Meridian.

    APPEARANCE: Features that defy species classification. Skin tone is a warm
    medium brown that could be human or synthetic -- no visible pores, but also
    no visible joint lines. Age is impossible to determine: could be 30, could
    be 300. Sharp, observant eyes in an unusual amber-gray that catch light
    strangely. A knowing half-smile that suggests they find the world endlessly
    amusing. Hair pulled back in a practical style, dark with a few strands
    that catch light in unexpected colors.

    CLOTHING: A deliberate mix of every species' fashion. A human-cut travelling
    coat in weathered leather, lined with fay-dyed fabric in deep forest green
    with patterns that shift in the light. A synthetic-precision buckle at the
    collar. Boots that have walked every biome. A satchel covered in patches
    and pins from different settlements. At their neck, a locket they never open.

    SETTING: Their Wandering Stall -- a mobile market stand set up at the edge
    of a cobblestone market square (Millhaven). The stall is a marvel of compact
    organization: shelves of curiosities, rare materials, and one-of-a-kind items.
    Colored canvas awning in deep red (#C0503A). Warm lantern light from a crystal
    lamp. Behind Ash, goods from every biome visible: a data crystal next to a
    jar of fay honey next to precision-milled synthetic components.

    POSE: Leaning casually against the stall counter, arms crossed, appraising
    the viewer with that unreadable smile. Completely at ease. The posture of
    someone who has been everywhere and is surprised by nothing.

    MOOD: World-weary kindness wrapped in mystery. Someone who knows more than
    they say and says more than they explain.

    PALETTE: Traveling merchant eclecticism against Millhaven market warmth.
    Weathered leather browns, fay greens, warm amber lantern light (#FFB347),
    cobblestone gray (#7A7A7A). The locket is a single point of polished gold.

    STYLE: Hand-painted with extra attention to the eyes -- they should draw the
    viewer in and refuse to give answers. The stall goods can be loosely rendered;
    Ash's face and hands need the detail.
  provider_options:
    aspect_ratio: "1:1"
    style: "natural"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1024
    height: 1024
    aspect_ratio: "1:1"

tags: [character, portrait, merchant, mystery, ambiguous, millhaven, npc, economy]
